# DEMEX — Gmail ingest credentials
# ---------------------------------
# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder) and fill in the two values below.
# The bridge loads .env automatically; .env is git-ignored so it never commits.
#
# HOW TO GET A GMAIL APP PASSWORD (one time):
#   1. Go to  https://myaccount.google.com/security
#   2. Turn ON "2-Step Verification" (App Passwords require it).
#   3. Open  https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#   4. App name: type "DEMEX"  ->  Create.
#   5. Google shows a 16-character password (e.g. "abcd efgh ijkl mnop").
#      Paste it below. Spaces are fine — they are stripped automatically.
#   6. This is NOT your normal Gmail password and can be revoked anytime.

DEMEX_GMAIL_USER=you@yourcompany.com
DEMEX_GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=abcd efgh ijkl mnop

# Anthropic API key for the in-app AI assistant (POST /api/ai).
# Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/ — leave blank to disable the
# AI endpoint (it returns 503 until a key is set).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
DEMEX_AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# Optional: change the bridge port (must match the URL you open).
# DEMEX_BRIDGE_PORT=8765

# Optional: extra folder (outside this project) that /api/takeoff is allowed
# to read plan PDFs from.
# DEMEX_PLANS_DIR=C:\Plans

# Folder where the daily inbox-sweep drop files (demex_itb_import_*.json)
# land, if different from the app folder. The desktop build sets this.
# DEMEX_IMPORTS_DIR=C:\Users\you\Desktop\DEMEX _ Claude\DEMEX

# --- GitHub backup (tools/github_backup.py; nightly on the server + "Back up now") ---
# 1. On GitHub create a PRIVATE, empty repo, e.g. shawnmziegaus-dd/DEMEX-data
# 2. github.com -> Settings -> Developer settings -> Fine-grained tokens -> Generate:
#    repository access = only that repo, permission Contents = Read and write.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_...
# GITHUB_BACKUP_REPO=shawnmziegaus-dd/DEMEX-data
# GITHUB_BACKUP_HOUR_UTC=6        (6 UTC = 2:00 am Eastern)
# GITHUB_BACKUP_MAX_MB=20         (skip single files larger than this)
# GITHUB_BACKUP_PDFS=1            (0 = index plan PDFs but do not upload them)

# --- Qualora ---
# If Qualora runs on its own server, /qualora/ forwards there. Otherwise place
# the Qualora page at apps/qualora/app.html and it is served from this server.
# QUALORA_URL=https://qualora.example.com
